WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.585
- Does it bother you that you
didn't get Rookie of the Year?

00:00:02.585 --> 00:00:04.838
- No, it doesn't bother me.
I blame myself.

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:07.716
- [Announcer:] Young circles,
floats. It hits.

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:09.342
- You're up here.
- I'm up here. I'm up here.

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:13.263
- Then you got to go
between your legs.

00:00:13.263 --> 00:00:15.265
- [Announcer:]
Three-pointer for Trae.

00:00:15.265 --> 00:00:17.642
- But OK. Honestly,
after that first game

00:00:17.642 --> 00:00:20.186
when you said it's over,
did you feel so silly?

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.063
- Oh, trust me.
- [Laughs]

00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:24.065
- Trust me.
I was sick.

00:00:24.065 --> 00:00:29.362
♪♪♪

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.989
- What's up, everybody?
It's Trae Young here

00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:33.158
with the Atlanta Hawks

00:00:33.158 --> 00:00:35.243
and your girl here
is back in A-Town,

00:00:35.243 --> 00:00:37.245
and I know she got
a lot of questions for me.

00:00:37.245 --> 00:00:38.496
So we're about to
"Take it There"

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:39.664
with Taylor Rooks.

00:00:39.664 --> 00:00:40.832
- [Announcer:]
Trae with the runner.

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:41.958
- [Announcer 2:]
Oh, my goodness,

00:00:41.958 --> 00:00:44.127
Trae getting 'em back
quickly.

00:00:44.127 --> 00:00:45.754
♪♪♪

00:00:45.754 --> 00:00:47.172
- [Taylor Rooks:] Thank you
for spending time with me

00:00:47.172 --> 00:00:48.631
after practice.

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:50.717
- Of course, of course.
- I'm happy to be back home.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.053
- I'm happy to be here with you,
so it's going to be fun.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.846
- Are you loving Atlanta?
- I love it.

00:00:54.846 --> 00:00:56.097
- Yeah.
- I love it here.

00:00:56.097 --> 00:00:57.640
- A lot of times people
say, like,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.101
you are the star Atlanta needs.

00:01:00.101 --> 00:01:02.562
What do you think they mean
when they say that about you?

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.022
- I mean, that excitement,

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:06.733
that kind of buzz,
that national attention,

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:09.110
and I just think they needed
someone to come in,

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:12.030
bring that fire back
to the city of Atlanta.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:14.824
- How wild is it though
to think, like,

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:17.952
if you continue this trajectory
that you're at right now...

00:01:17.952 --> 00:01:19.579
- Mmhmm.
- Like, your name is with,

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:22.040
like, the Dominiques.
- Yeah, that's, it's crazy.

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:23.750
- Yeah.
- It's crazy to think sometimes.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.835
It's like,
I look up at the rafters,

00:01:25.835 --> 00:01:27.921
like, in our gym and you see
Pistol Pete,

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.215
you see Dominique,
you see legends

00:01:30.215 --> 00:01:32.926
and then people tell me
all the time, if I stay healthy

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.887
and things go my way
and continue this way,

00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:39.390
that one day my, my jersey
could be hanging up there.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.184
- Now it is no secret.

00:01:41.184 --> 00:01:43.728
Anybody who follows me knows
I go very hard for the Hawks.

00:01:43.728 --> 00:01:44.979
- Mmhmm.
- I am a Hawks fan.

00:01:44.979 --> 00:01:46.773
- [Laughs]
- The thing, though,

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.108
that whenever
I talk about the Hawks,

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.527
people are like,
"They're losing.

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:52.987
They're not even that good."
But I'm like, we're young.

00:01:52.987 --> 00:01:54.864
- Yeah.
- Like, we're figuring it out.

00:01:54.864 --> 00:01:58.493
But how long can
"We're young"

00:01:58.493 --> 00:02:00.370
be an excuse for losing?

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:01.996
- Not very long.
Not very long.

00:02:01.996 --> 00:02:03.832
I think if you look
at our team though,

00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:07.168
we've started five guys
22 and younger.

00:02:07.168 --> 00:02:08.753
So it's not an excuse
by any means,

00:02:08.753 --> 00:02:10.880
but it's just reality,
to be honest with you.

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:12.423
Trust me, it'll change soon.

00:02:12.423 --> 00:02:13.925
♪♪♪

00:02:13.925 --> 00:02:15.426
- [Taylor:] So let's talk about
draft night.

00:02:15.426 --> 00:02:17.470
- [Trae Young:] Mmhmm.
- Obviously that is a night

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.681
that has got to stay
with you forever.

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:21.057
- Yeah.
- Give me a play-by-play

00:02:21.057 --> 00:02:23.059
of how the day and night
happened.

00:02:23.059 --> 00:02:25.770
- I remember looking on TV,
just wanted to see

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.689
what people were thinking about
where I was going to go,

00:02:27.689 --> 00:02:30.775
and I was looking at everybody
saying I was going to go 12, 14.

00:02:30.775 --> 00:02:32.360
I was talking to my agent
like, "Is this for real?"

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:33.862
He's just like,
"Man, turn off everything."

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:35.989
Get to the draft.
Sitting down at the table,

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.740
third pick's about to get
called, it's Atlanta.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.367
The commissioner comes out
and they say,

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:41.703
"Luka Doncic is the third pick."

00:02:41.703 --> 00:02:43.746
So as he's walking
across the stage,

00:02:43.746 --> 00:02:46.040
my dad's sitting next to me
and my agent's right behind me.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:49.335
They come up and they say,
"You're going to Atlanta."

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.462
I said, "What do you mean?
They didn't, like,

00:02:51.462 --> 00:02:52.797
they didn't just call me."

00:02:52.797 --> 00:02:54.174
- [Taylor:] So you didn't know
till right there.

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:55.216
- [Trae:] I didn't know till
right there,

00:02:55.216 --> 00:02:57.635
but all day my dad
and my agent,

00:02:57.635 --> 00:02:59.721
they knew that they were
going to trade up for me,

00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:01.514
and I was still confused.

00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.309
And so my hands were
sweating so hard.

00:03:04.309 --> 00:03:06.394
And when the fourth pick
got called,

00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:09.189
Memphis was called,
and I was, like, crying.

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:12.984
Like, I was nervous, didn't know
how I was going to react.

00:03:12.984 --> 00:03:15.403
Didn't want to trip up
the steps going up.

00:03:15.403 --> 00:03:19.365
And then they announced my name,
and then I got across the stage,

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.242
got down,
talked to Maria Taylor,

00:03:21.242 --> 00:03:22.869
and she was just telling me,
yeah,

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:24.871
they just traded me to Atlanta.

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.331
- [Taylor:] So when you
look at that night,

00:03:26.331 --> 00:03:28.041
are you like, "OK,
I wish they would have

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.918
told me earlier in the day,"
or are you happy with how it...

00:03:29.918 --> 00:03:32.212
- I'm happy with how, I'm happy
with how it happened.

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:37.008
I think if I'd have known, maybe
I wouldn't have been so nervous,

00:03:37.008 --> 00:03:39.427
but I don't think I would've
really appreciated

00:03:39.427 --> 00:03:40.678
the moment like I did,

00:03:40.678 --> 00:03:42.055
so it was cool.
- Mmhmm.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:48.645
You know, if I was you,
I would be so annoyed

00:03:48.645 --> 00:03:51.064
with the constant
Luka/Trae talk.

00:03:51.064 --> 00:03:52.232
- [Trae:] Yeah.
- [Taylor:] Just because

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:53.733
you're going
to be tied forever.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.902
And I mean, I don't know
if you can really help it.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.320
But does it bother you that

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.197
that's what it's always
going to be?

00:03:59.197 --> 00:04:00.448
- Uh...

00:04:00.448 --> 00:04:03.326
I mean, to be honest with you,
like, it's annoying,

00:04:03.326 --> 00:04:04.744
but it's going to be,
it's going to be that way

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.496
until we're both,
we're both done playing.

00:04:06.496 --> 00:04:08.915
So might as well
just embrace it.

00:04:08.915 --> 00:04:11.751
- [Announcer:] Long deep three
over Deandre Ayton.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:13.294
- [Announcer 2:]
He is never out of range.

00:04:13.294 --> 00:04:15.755
- [Taylor:] With the way
basketball has evolved,

00:04:15.755 --> 00:04:17.340
should we move
the three-point line?

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:20.134
- I think maybe we should add
a four-point line.

00:04:20.134 --> 00:04:21.386
- Ooh!

00:04:21.386 --> 00:04:23.096
- [Trae:]
I think that'd be,

00:04:23.096 --> 00:04:25.098
I think that would change
the game up a little bit.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:27.308
And the way guys
are hitting half-court shots,

00:04:27.308 --> 00:04:30.979
making that four points,
maybe that'd be cool.

00:04:30.979 --> 00:04:32.230
- [Taylor:]
Does it bother you

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:33.856
that you didn't get
Rookie of the Year?

00:04:33.856 --> 00:04:36.442
- No, it didn't bother me.
It doesn't bother me too much.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:40.571
I blame myself for, for not
getting Rookie of the Year.

00:04:40.571 --> 00:04:43.074
I didn't put myself
in the best situation early on,

00:04:43.074 --> 00:04:46.953
the way I started,
and I came on super hot late,

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:50.206
but it was already too late.
I mean, so for me,

00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:52.834
I can't really be mad
at anybody besides myself.

00:04:52.834 --> 00:04:55.336
- No, I will say obviously
I follow a lot of

00:04:55.336 --> 00:04:57.255
Hawks people on Twitter.

00:04:57.255 --> 00:04:59.716
Your first year, there were
some shaky moments.

00:04:59.716 --> 00:05:01.467
- Mmhmm.
- And there was a lot of people

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:04.887
that were like, "All right,
should've got Luka."

00:05:04.887 --> 00:05:06.055
- Yeah.

00:05:06.055 --> 00:05:08.725
- What did you think
when that was happening?

00:05:08.725 --> 00:05:10.018
- Just wait,
it's going to change.

00:05:10.018 --> 00:05:12.020
It's going to,
it's going to be better.

00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:14.230
Even when I had
my struggling moments,

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.899
I think everybody really,
really overreacted.

00:05:16.899 --> 00:05:19.110
I remember I, I didn't shoot
very well my first game,

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.611
and it was all
on SportsCenter,

00:05:20.611 --> 00:05:22.613
all everybody could talk about
on all the sports channels

00:05:22.613 --> 00:05:27.035
is just, I mean, how major
of a bust I could be.

00:05:27.035 --> 00:05:28.244
I just took it
with a grain of salt

00:05:28.244 --> 00:05:30.580
and just wanted people
to keep that same energy

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:33.624
when it turned over, so that's,
that's how I looked at it.

00:05:33.624 --> 00:05:36.627
- Your iconic tweet,
of course, was,

00:05:36.627 --> 00:05:39.505
the apology should be as loud
as the disrespect was.

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:40.673
- Mm-hmm.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:43.176
- Have the apologies been
as loud?

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.552
- They were, they were loud.

00:05:44.552 --> 00:05:46.888
There's never going to be
100% people on your side.

00:05:46.888 --> 00:05:48.389
- Was there a game for you
where you were like,

00:05:48.389 --> 00:05:50.183
"This is it.
This is the turning point"?

00:05:50.183 --> 00:05:52.977
- When we played in Denver,
had some guys out,

00:05:52.977 --> 00:05:55.813
whenever our third best player
got hurt.

00:05:55.813 --> 00:05:58.983
John was out for me
to go off in Denver

00:05:58.983 --> 00:06:02.487
against a really good team
and get a win on the road.

00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:05.531
I think that was, like, one of
those moments where it's like,

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.158
"All right, like,
I can do this."

00:06:07.158 --> 00:06:09.077
- You do have some vets
on this team,

00:06:09.077 --> 00:06:11.454
but it's not like you have
a super strong vet core.

00:06:11.454 --> 00:06:13.122
- Yeah. Yeah.
- Vet presence on this team.

00:06:13.122 --> 00:06:15.583
- Who do you lean on
in the NBA?

00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:18.294
- A guy like Chris Paul.

00:06:18.294 --> 00:06:20.296
Growing up,
going to Thunder games,

00:06:20.296 --> 00:06:24.258
I've known and talked
to KD, Russ.

00:06:24.258 --> 00:06:26.928
Those are my guys, those are
my guys I could really,

00:06:26.928 --> 00:06:30.098
I can call,
talk to, ask for advice.

00:06:30.098 --> 00:06:31.849
- What is the best
piece of advice

00:06:31.849 --> 00:06:33.059
that Chris Paul has given you?

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:35.103
- Stay aggressive.

00:06:35.103 --> 00:06:38.189
He, I remember after
we played 'em last year,

00:06:38.189 --> 00:06:40.483
my rookie year, just
I played really well out there

00:06:40.483 --> 00:06:42.568
and he just,
he wants me to just continue

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.654
to be aggressive, just always be
in attack mode

00:06:44.654 --> 00:06:47.657
in wanting just to score,
just to be in attack mode

00:06:47.657 --> 00:06:49.700
to get other people involved,
whatever it was.

00:06:49.700 --> 00:06:51.077
- And what's the best
piece of advice

00:06:51.077 --> 00:06:52.703
that Russell Westbrook
has given you?

00:06:52.703 --> 00:06:55.957
- [Trae:] Uh, Russ has given me
a lot of advice over the years.

00:06:55.957 --> 00:06:57.583
I remember when I was a kid,

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.460
um, I was going to
a Thunder game.

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.921
He walked out
with some crazy clothes on,

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:04.924
which he always does,
but I asked him about some,

00:07:04.924 --> 00:07:06.300
some clothes he had on,
and he said,

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:07.844
"Maybe one day
you can get some of these."

00:07:07.844 --> 00:07:09.137
It was, I think
at the time it was

00:07:09.137 --> 00:07:10.721
Christian, like, Louboutins,

00:07:10.721 --> 00:07:13.182
and it was some spiked shoes
with the red bottoms.

00:07:13.182 --> 00:07:15.435
So I'll never forget that,
and, uh...

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:16.853
I think after we played 'em
this year,

00:07:16.853 --> 00:07:20.606
he was telling you about his,
his first year in the league,

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:22.775
they lost 27 games in a row.

00:07:22.775 --> 00:07:25.403
So it's like,
just to stay with it,

00:07:25.403 --> 00:07:27.113
just be that leader
on my team.

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.030
- [Announcer:]
That's his range.

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:29.574
- [Announcer 2:]
And Young from center court!

00:07:29.574 --> 00:07:30.992
Yes!
[Cheering]

00:07:30.992 --> 00:07:32.243
- [Taylor:] You being
an all-star

00:07:32.243 --> 00:07:34.245
is kind of a debate around

00:07:34.245 --> 00:07:37.582
because the Hawks
are a "losing team."

00:07:37.582 --> 00:07:39.584
I even got into a fight
about this on my Twitter show...

00:07:39.584 --> 00:07:41.377
- I'm sorry.
- But that's a different story.

00:07:41.377 --> 00:07:45.756
Um, what should be the criteria
of being an all-star?

00:07:45.756 --> 00:07:46.716
- I've always been taught

00:07:46.716 --> 00:07:47.967
winning takes care
of everything.

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.303
So my main focus coming
into a season is winning.

00:07:50.303 --> 00:07:53.181
But I think with this year's
criteria,

00:07:53.181 --> 00:07:55.850
people are, or were mad,

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:59.312
but I was first in fan voting,

00:07:59.312 --> 00:08:02.857
I was second in, um,
the media,

00:08:02.857 --> 00:08:04.734
and then I was third in peers.

00:08:04.734 --> 00:08:06.777
So it's like, I don't know
what people, like,

00:08:06.777 --> 00:08:08.237
should be mad about.

00:08:08.237 --> 00:08:11.741
- Tell me your favorite all-star
moment that we don't know about.

00:08:11.741 --> 00:08:14.994
- Oh, favorite all-star moment.

00:08:14.994 --> 00:08:16.996
I mean, I think people
saw me and Giannis.

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:19.540
I was telling him
how he'd be traveling

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.000
and all this stuff on his euros,

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.669
and I thought he picked up
the ball before he took his,

00:08:23.669 --> 00:08:26.672
his step with his left foot,
and then he'd take a euro.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:28.382
It's quick, [snaps fingers]
but, like,

00:08:28.382 --> 00:08:31.469
whenever he demonstrates it
to you slowly,

00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:33.346
you understand
why it's not travelling.

00:08:33.346 --> 00:08:34.889
♪♪♪

00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:36.516
- [Taylor:] Nutmeg time.
- [Trae:] Nutmeg time?

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:38.434
- Aight, bet.
- How did you learn the nutmeg?

00:08:38.434 --> 00:08:40.770
- [Trae:] I was, I always, like,
do it with my dad,

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:43.105
messing around or whatever,
and he would always do it on me.

00:08:43.105 --> 00:08:44.857
- So you play defense.
- All right.

00:08:44.857 --> 00:08:46.484
- I always got to relax you.
- OK.

00:08:46.484 --> 00:08:48.194
- Make you not, uh...
- But I'm up here.

00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:49.654
- You up here?
- I'm up here.

00:08:49.654 --> 00:08:50.988
I'm up here.
- Then you got to

00:08:50.988 --> 00:08:52.448
go between your legs.
- [Laughs]

00:08:52.448 --> 00:08:54.033
- I did it in the
All-Star Game with James.

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:55.535
- You did, but you did
like a,

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:56.911
it was crazy.
- [Trae:] He was turning...

00:08:56.911 --> 00:08:57.995
- [Taylor:] Yeah.
- [Trae:] ...so he was,

00:08:57.995 --> 00:08:59.413
I was driving, so if you're
guarding me...

00:08:59.413 --> 00:09:00.623
- Uh huh.
- ...and you're turning...

00:09:00.623 --> 00:09:01.874
I'd always...
- Turning this way?

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:04.252
- [Trae:] I'd do it.
That's how I got the lay-up

00:09:04.252 --> 00:09:05.920
or whatever, but...
- [Taylor:] OK.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:08.422
And it's funny because even
when you did it to James, right?

00:09:08.422 --> 00:09:10.091
Like you nutmeg him
and then he tries to,

00:09:10.091 --> 00:09:11.634
like, do this,
but it's too late.

00:09:11.634 --> 00:09:13.844
- Yeah, it's too late, it's too
late before you realize it.

00:09:13.844 --> 00:09:15.388
- [Taylor:] OK.
Is there anybody

00:09:15.388 --> 00:09:17.598
you want to nutmeg
that you haven't yet?

